This is pretty close to a system along the lines I was thinking of.

I started thinking about it, and this is what I came up with:

You could divide magic up into these aspects:

constructive/destructive
earth/fire/water/air
concentrated/dispersed

So, magic missle might be a concentrated destructive air spell. Stinking
cloud might be the same, except dispersed. Wizard Lock might be constructed,
concentrated earth.

Maybe you could 'load' the spell with mana, for stronger effects. Each spell
might have a minimum mana requirement.

Keep in mind this is just a preliminary idea. Sort of mental stretching.



